node_modules/
.expo/
*.log
*.log.*
*.db
*.db-*

# iOS generated artifacts must never be uploaded to EAS.
ios/Pods/
ios/build/
ios/build-*/
ios/**/*.xcuserdata/
ios/**/*.xcuserstate
ios/**/DerivedData/
ios/.xcode.env.local

# Everything below this line is repo-root cleanup, and it only matters when the
# build is run WITHOUT EAS_NO_VCS=1. Read this before touching it.
#
# mobile-native/ sits inside the CoinPilotX git repo, so by default eas-cli
# picks its Git VCS client, roots the archive at the *repo* root, and builds the
# tarball from `git archive HEAD` — which consults .gitignore and ignores
# .easignore entirely. That is why the archive was 251 MB (≈ the 281 MB of
# tracked files, compressed) and died mid-upload with `write EPIPE` at 213 MB,
# and why two rounds of edits to this file changed the size by exactly zero.
# Naming offenders individually did nothing; so did inverting to "/*" plus
# "!/mobile-native" (gitignore cannot re-include a path whose parent directory
# is excluded).
#
# The fix is to bypass the VCS client:
#
#     EAS_NO_VCS=1 npx eas-cli build --platform ios --profile production
#
# That switches eas-cli to a filesystem walk rooted at mobile-native/, which
# does honour .easignore — archive drops to 66 MB and uploads cleanly. The
# trade-off is that uncommitted working-tree changes are included, so commit
# first if you want the archive to match a SHA.
#
# The root-level entries below are therefore belt-and-braces for anyone who
# forgets the env var. An iOS build needs nothing from this repo outside
# mobile-native/, so anything new at the root belongs in this list.
#
# HAZARD — these are bare names, not anchored paths, so under EAS_NO_VCS=1
# (archive root = mobile-native/) each one ALSO matches mobile-native/<name>.
# `scripts/` collided exactly that way: package.json's postinstall is
# `bash scripts/apply-native-patches.sh`, which applies the Hermes
# react-native+0.81.5 patch, so excluding it breaks the EAS build. It is
# re-negated at the bottom of this file. Before adding a name here, check that
# mobile-native/ has no directory by that name — and if it ever grows one, add a
# matching "!" line down there too.
.git/
services/
tests/
scripts/
backups/
backend/
static/
templates/
migrations/
models/
seo/
data/
outputs/
logs/
certificates/
pulse_communications_v2/
.fuse_hidden*
*.pyc
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
reports/
release-assets/
mobile/
storage/
static/uploads/
CoinPilotX:screenshots:/
.undx/
.undx_*_workspace/
__pycache__/
**/__pycache__/
mobile-native/node_modules/
mobile-native/.expo/
mobile-native/ios/Pods/
mobile-native/ios/build/
mobile-native/ios/build-*/
mobile-native/ios/**/*.xcuserdata/
mobile-native/ios/**/*.xcuserstate
mobile-native/ios/**/DerivedData/
mobile-native/ios/.xcode.env.local

# Re-include the app's own scripts/ — see the HAZARD note above. Costs ~40 KB
# under EAS_NO_VCS=1 and ~3 MB in the (unused) repo-root mode; either is cheap
# next to shipping an unpatched binary.
!scripts/
!scripts/**
